  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "While hunting a method to delay aperture calamities and tribulations, Fang Yuan locks onto this immortal killer move. The name suggests one day inside becomes the length of a year, but Hei Fan notes that full day-to-year extension is only theoretical and the real effect varies with path dao marks and blessed land grade.",
      "chapters": [
        1130
      ],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_killer_moves",
        "char_hei_fan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "It sits in a set of four aperture-rate moves with months pass like years (slow; month Gu supplements), years pass like months, and years pass like days (both accelerate). Slowing aperture time spaces calamities and tribulations farther apart in outside-world time; Fang Yuan’s example is shifting a two-month tribulation cycle toward decades or even a century. Tradeoffs include slower resource growth and cultivation progress. Hei Fan adds that immortal day Gu or month Gu would cut the mortal Gu cost and raise the effect.",
      "chapters": [
        1130
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_month_gu",
        "gu_day_gu",
        "sys_mortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After annexing Han Dong blessed land, Fang Yuan casts the move inside his cloud city in Lang Ya blessed land. Gu worms fill the sky, green grape immortal essence is spent, light fills the sovereign immortal aperture, and the tributary of the River of Time shrinks and thins as the aperture rate of time slows and tribulation intervals lengthen.",
      "chapters": [
        1187
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "first-cast",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_han_dong_blessed_land",
        "loc_lang_ya_blessed_land",
        "sys_gu_worms",
        "loc_tributary_of_the_river_of_time"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hei Fan had wanted immortal day Gu and month Gu so casts of days pass like years and similar moves would not burn so many mortal day Gu and month Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        1200
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "first-cast",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hei Fan’s time path true inheritance notes that days pass like years and months pass like years share a problem when modifying the tributary of the River of Time to change the rate of time.",
      "chapters": [
        1416
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "first-cast",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Later, such moves still expend immortal essence and, after each use, lose influence on that tributary for a set interval.",
      "chapters": [
        1612
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "first-cast",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
